      "source": [
        "# Splines de suavizamiento\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "Recapitulando: en las secciones anteriores construimos modelos flexibles utilizando regresión polinómica, funciones escalonadas, funciones base y splines de regresión.\n",
        "\n",
        "En un **spline de regresión**, una decisión importante consiste en determinar el número y la posición de los nodos (*knots*).\n",
        "\n",
        "Los **splines de suavizamiento** (*smoothing splines*) utilizan una estrategia diferente. En lugar de controlar la flexibilidad seleccionando explícitamente un pequeño conjunto de nodos, buscamos una función $g(x)$ que logre un equilibrio entre:\n",
        "\n",
        "- ajustarse bien a los datos;\n",
        "- mantenerse suficientemente suave.\n",
        "\n",
        "Matemáticamente, buscamos una función que minimice\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\n",
        "\\left(y_i-g(x_i)\\right)^2\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\lambda\n",
        "\\int\n",
        "\\left[g''(t)\\right]^2dt.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "El primer término mide el error de ajuste, mientras que el segundo penaliza funciones demasiado irregulares.\n",
        "\n",
        "El parámetro $\\lambda$ controla el compromiso entre ambos objetivos:\n",
        "\n",
        "- valores pequeños de $\\lambda$ permiten ajustes más flexibles;\n",
        "- valores grandes de $\\lambda$ producen curvas más suaves.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Librerías\n",
        "\n",
        "Comenzamos importando las bibliotecas necesarias."
      ],
      "id": "3ad2de6e"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "\n",
        "from ISLP import load_data\n",
        "from pygam import LinearGAM, s"
      ],
      "id": "2f048eae",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "La biblioteca `pygam` permite ajustar modelos aditivos generalizados o **GAMs** (*Generalized Additive Models*).\n",
        "\n",
        "Un spline de suavizamiento con un único predictor puede verse como un caso particular de un GAM. Por ahora utilizaremos `pygam` únicamente para estudiar splines de suavizamiento.\n",
        "\n",
        "Los GAMs con varios predictores y diferentes tipos de términos los estudiaremos más adelante.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Cargar los datos\n",
        "\n",
        "Utilizaremos nuevamente el conjunto de datos `Wage`."
      ],
      "id": "8f2b498e"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Wage = load_data(\"Wage\")\n",
        "\n",
        "Wage.head()"
      ],
      "id": "adff3189",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Nos interesa estudiar la relación entre:\n",
        "\n",
        "- `age`: edad del trabajador;\n",
        "- `wage`: salario.\n",
        "\n",
        "Extraemos estas dos variables."
      ],
      "id": "85c2f1b9"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "age = Wage[\"age\"]\n",
        "y = Wage[\"wage\"]"
      ],
      "id": "99dbef6a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Podemos visualizar los datos originales."
      ],
      "id": "adf1f2b6"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(9, 6))\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.scatter(\n",
        "    age,\n",
        "    y,\n",
        "    alpha=0.3\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Edad\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Salario\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Relación entre edad y salario\")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "9c0e95be",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "La relación no parece completamente lineal. El salario parece aumentar durante las primeras décadas de la vida laboral y posteriormente estabilizarse o disminuir.\n",
        "\n",
        "Nuestro objetivo será modelar esta relación mediante una curva suave.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Preparar el predictor para `pygam`\n",
        "\n",
        "`pygam` espera que los predictores se proporcionen en forma de una **matriz**.\n",
        "\n",
        "Actualmente `age` es un vector:"
      ],
      "id": "83db3221"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "np.asarray(age).shape"
      ],
      "id": "9c6a8c56",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Lo transformamos en una matriz con una sola columna."
      ],
      "id": "d1ef08d1"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "X_age = np.asarray(age).reshape(-1, 1)"
      ],
      "id": "4a9a9d56",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Ahora podemos revisar sus dimensiones."
      ],
      "id": "f90d3bf6"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "X_age.shape"
      ],
      "id": "03174d2a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "La instrucción\n",
        "\n",
        "```python\n",
        "reshape(-1, 1)\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "indica que queremos construir una matriz con:\n",
        "\n",
        "- una columna;\n",
        "- tantas filas como sean necesarias.\n",
        "\n",
        "Por ejemplo, un vector\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "(20,30,40,50)\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "se transforma conceptualmente en\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\begin{pmatrix}\n",
        "20\\\\\n",
        "30\\\\\n",
        "40\\\\\n",
        "50\n",
        "\\end{pmatrix}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Esto no cambia los datos; solamente cambia la forma en la que están organizados.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Nuestro primer spline de suavizamiento\n",
        "\n",
        "Construiremos un primer modelo."
      ],
      "id": "e6be2a03"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "gam = LinearGAM(\n",
        "    s(0, lam=0.6)\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "gam.fit(X_age, y)"
      ],
      "id": "6dfe7348",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Veamos las partes de esta instrucción.\n",
        "\n",
        "### `LinearGAM()`\n",
        "\n",
        "`LinearGAM()` utiliza una función de pérdida basada en errores cuadrados, por lo que es apropiado cuando la variable respuesta es cuantitativa.\n",
        "\n",
        "En nuestro caso:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "Y=\\text{wage}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "### `s(0)`\n",
        "\n",
        "La función\n",
        "\n",
        "```python\n",
        "s(0)\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "indica que queremos modelar la primera columna de la matriz $X$ mediante un término suave.\n",
        "\n",
        "Como `X_age` solamente contiene una columna,\n",
        "\n",
        "```python\n",
        "s(0)\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "corresponde a `age`.\n",
        "\n",
        "### `lam`\n",
        "\n",
        "El argumento\n",
        "\n",
        "```python\n",
        "lam=0.6\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "corresponde al parámetro de penalización $\\lambda$ que estudiamos anteriormente.\n",
        "\n",
        "Por tanto, `pygam` está resolviendo numéricamente un problema que busca equilibrar ajuste y suavidad.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Construir valores para realizar predicciones\n",
        "\n",
        "Para visualizar el modelo no queremos obtener predicciones únicamente en las edades observadas.\n",
        "\n",
        "Construiremos una secuencia de edades desde la edad mínima hasta la máxima."
      ],
      "id": "b47b5156"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "age_grid = np.linspace(\n",
        "    age.min(),\n",
        "    age.max(),\n",
        "    500\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "c7fe168c",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Para utilizar estos valores con `pygam`, también debemos convertirlos en una matriz."
      ],
      "id": "d7cbea8f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "age_grid_matrix = age_grid.reshape(-1, 1)"
      ],
      "id": "69fa7f54",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Ahora calculamos las predicciones."
      ],
      "id": "76cc259b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "pred = gam.predict(age_grid_matrix)"
      ],
      "id": "57bae372",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Visualizar el spline\n",
        "\n",
        "Podemos representar simultáneamente los datos y la curva estimada."
      ],
      "id": "996ded03"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(9, 6))\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.scatter(\n",
        "    age,\n",
        "    y,\n",
        "    alpha=0.3\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.plot(\n",
        "    age_grid,\n",
        "    pred,\n",
        "    linewidth=3\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Edad\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Salario\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Spline de suavizamiento\")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "73dc7451",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "La curva resultante es suave y permite capturar una relación no lineal entre edad y salario.\n",
        "\n",
        "Sin embargo, esta curva depende del valor elegido para $\\lambda$.\n",
        "\n",
        "La pregunta ahora es:\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        ":::: {.callout-warning icon=\"false\"}\n",
        "## 🧠 Pregunta\n",
        "¿qué ocurre si cambiamos $\\lambda$?\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-tip collapse=\"true\" icon=\"false\"}\n",
        "## Solución\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Efecto del parámetro $\\lambda$\n",
        "\n",
        "Recordemos que el modelo minimiza una expresión de la forma\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\text{Error de ajuste}\n",
        "+\n",
        "\\lambda\n",
        "\\left(\\text{penalización por rugosidad}\\right).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Por tanto, esperamos que:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\lambda\\downarrow\n",
        "\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n",
        "\\text{mayor flexibilidad},\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "mientras que\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\lambda\\uparrow\n",
        "\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n",
        "\\text{mayor suavidad}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Vamos a comprobarlo empíricamente.\n",
        "\n",
        "Consideraremos valores de $\\lambda$ desde\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "10^{-2}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "hasta\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "10^6.\n",
        "$$"
      ],
      "id": "f671f075"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "lambdas = np.logspace(-2, 6, 5)\n",
        "\n",
        "lambdas"
      ],
      "id": "f4ffebad",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "La función `np.logspace()` construye valores igualmente espaciados en una escala logarítmica.\n",
        "\n",
        "Esto resulta útil porque queremos comparar valores de $\\lambda$ que difieren por varios órdenes de magnitud.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Comparar diferentes valores de $\\lambda$\n",
        "\n",
        "Ajustaremos un spline diferente para cada valor de $\\lambda$."
      ],
      "id": "ec5f09ff"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 7))\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.scatter(\n",
        "    age,\n",
        "    y,\n",
        "    alpha=0.25\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "for lam in lambdas:\n",
        "\n",
        "    gam_lam = LinearGAM(\n",
        "        s(0, lam=lam)\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    gam_lam.fit(X_age, y)\n",
        "\n",
        "    pred_lam = gam_lam.predict(age_grid_matrix)\n",
        "\n",
        "    plt.plot(\n",
        "        age_grid,\n",
        "        pred_lam,\n",
        "        linewidth=2,\n",
        "        label=fr\"$\\lambda={lam:.0e}$\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Edad\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Salario\")\n",
        "plt.title(r\"Efecto del parámetro $\\lambda$\")\n",
        "plt.legend()\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "4d7ca3ab",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Observen cuidadosamente cómo cambia la forma de la curva.\n",
        "\n",
        "Cuando $\\lambda$ es pequeño, la penalización tiene poca importancia y el modelo puede adaptarse más a los datos.\n",
        "\n",
        "Cuando $\\lambda$ aumenta, la penalización adquiere mayor peso y la curva se vuelve progresivamente más suave.\n",
        "\n",
        "Para valores suficientemente grandes de $\\lambda$, el ajuste comienza a aproximarse a una relación lineal.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## $\\lambda$ y complejidad del modelo\n",
        "\n",
        "El número de parámetros de un spline de suavizamiento no describe directamente su complejidad.\n",
        "\n",
        "Por ello utilizamos los **grados de libertad efectivos**.\n",
        "\n",
        "La relación general es\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\lambda\\uparrow\n",
        "\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n",
        "df_\\lambda\\downarrow.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Es decir:\n",
        "\n",
        "- $\\lambda$ pequeño $\\rightarrow$ más grados de libertad efectivos;\n",
        "- $\\lambda$ grande $\\rightarrow$ menos grados de libertad efectivos.\n",
        "\n",
        "Esto conecta directamente con el compromiso sesgo-varianza:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\text{mayor flexibilidad}\n",
        "\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n",
        "\\text{menor sesgo y mayor varianza},\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "mientras que\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\text{menor flexibilidad}\n",
        "\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n",
        "\\text{mayor sesgo y menor varianza}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## ¿Cómo elegimos $\\lambda$?\n",
        "\n",
        "Hasta ahora hemos elegido $\\lambda$ manualmente.\n",
        "\n",
        "Por ejemplo:\n",
        "\n",
        "```python\n",
        "lam=0.6\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "Pero no existe una razón particular para pensar que ese valor sea el mejor para nuestros datos.\n",
        "\n",
        "Una estrategia más adecuada consiste en seleccionar $\\lambda$ utilizando los propios datos.\n",
        "\n",
        "`pygam` proporciona el método\n",
        "\n",
        "```python\n",
        "gridsearch()\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "para realizar esta búsqueda.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "##  Búsqueda de $\\lambda$\n",
        "\n",
        "Primero definimos una colección de posibles valores."
      ],
      "id": "30790be7"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "lam_grid = np.logspace(-3, 5, 30)"
      ],
      "id": "893b59be",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Ahora realizamos la búsqueda."
      ],
      "id": "d06e966f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "gam_opt = LinearGAM(\n",
        "    s(0)\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "gam_opt.gridsearch(\n",
        "    X_age,\n",
        "    y,\n",
        "    lam=lam_grid,\n",
        "    progress=False\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "295e7319",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "`gridsearch()` ajusta modelos utilizando diferentes valores del parámetro de suavizamiento y selecciona una opción de acuerdo con el criterio utilizado internamente por `pygam`.\n",
        "\n",
        "Podemos consultar el valor seleccionado."
      ],
      "id": "65c7c9d9"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "gam_opt.lam"
      ],
      "id": "3e6f2023",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Es importante distinguir entre dos ideas:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **explorar manualmente $\\lambda$**, para comprender su efecto sobre la curva;\n",
        "2. **seleccionar $\\lambda$ mediante un criterio basado en los datos**, para construir el modelo final.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Comparar un valor arbitrario con el valor seleccionado\n",
        "\n",
        "Comparemos el modelo inicial, que utilizaba\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\lambda=0.6,\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "con el modelo obtenido mediante la búsqueda."
      ],
      "id": "26800f7c"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "pred_default = gam.predict(age_grid_matrix)\n",
        "pred_opt = gam_opt.predict(age_grid_matrix)\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 7))\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.scatter(\n",
        "    age,\n",
        "    y,\n",
        "    alpha=0.25\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.plot(\n",
        "    age_grid,\n",
        "    pred_default,\n",
        "    linewidth=3,\n",
        "    label=r\"$\\lambda=0.6$\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.plot(\n",
        "    age_grid,\n",
        "    pred_opt,\n",
        "    linewidth=3,\n",
        "    label=\"Lambda seleccionado\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.xlabel(\"Edad\")\n",
        "plt.ylabel(\"Salario\")\n",
        "plt.title(\"Comparación de splines de suavizamiento\")\n",
        "plt.legend()\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "c3f54ab5",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Dos valores diferentes de $\\lambda$ no necesariamente producen curvas visualmente muy diferentes.\n",
        "\n",
        "Esto es importante: aumentar la complejidad del modelo solamente tiene sentido si los datos proporcionan evidencia de que esa complejidad adicional es útil.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Grados de libertad efectivos del modelo\n",
        "\n",
        "Recordemos que teóricamente los grados de libertad efectivos pueden escribirse como\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "df_\\lambda\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\operatorname{tr}(S_\\lambda).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "No corresponden simplemente al número de coeficientes almacenados en el modelo.\n",
        "\n",
        "Representan la **flexibilidad efectiva** que queda después de aplicar la penalización.\n",
        "\n",
        "`pygam` calcula esta cantidad durante el ajuste.\n",
        "\n",
        "Podemos inspeccionarla mediante:"
      ],
      "id": "8f3903a9"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "gam_opt.statistics_[\"edof\"]"
      ],
      "id": "e6cdf678",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
